---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE, withBase } from "../lib/site";

const description =
  "Affiliate, sponsor, and privacy disclosures for Tried This Week. Verdicts cannot be bought. Sponsored items and affiliate links will be labeled when they exist. None are live yet.";
---

<Base title="Disclosures" description={description} path="/disclosures/">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">Legal and money</p>
      <h1>How we will handle sponsors, affiliates, and your email.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        This page is the source of truth for money and tracking on {SITE.name}. If a practice here
        and a line in an issue ever disagree, this page wins until we correct the issue.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>The newsletter is live. Signups are handled by Beehiiv.</strong>
        We do not have sponsors or affiliate links yet. When those exist, they will be labeled. A
        payment, a gift, or a free account cannot buy a Keep verdict or hide a Drop.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising and sponsors</h2>
      <p>
        A future issue may include one clearly labeled sponsor slot, kept out of the verdict. The
        word “Sponsored” will appear on the placement in the email and on the web. Sponsor copy is
        not a lab result. We will not present a paid placement as a Tried card.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not plan to sell sponsor slots until the list has a real, engaged readership and a few
        clean issues with click data. Until then, there is nothing to buy.
      </p>

      <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
      <p>
        Some tool links may later use affiliate programs. If a link can earn a commission, it will
        be marked as an affiliate link on the issue and, where practical, on the link itself. We
        will only affiliate tools we have actually tried, and only after a program is approved.
        Free trials often do not pay, and refunds can claw back commissions — we will not pretend
        otherwise.
      </p>
      <p>
        As of the launch of this site, <strong>there are no affiliate links</strong> on {SITE.name}.
      </p>

      <h2>Independence of verdicts</h2>
      <p>
        Keep and Drop are editorial. They describe a specific job and stack, not a global ranking.
        A vendor cannot pay to change a stamp. If we made a factual error, we will correct it in
        public.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy and the signup form</h2>
      <p>
        Newsletter signups are handled by <strong>Beehiiv</strong>. The form on the home page is a
        Beehiiv embed. When you subscribe, Beehiiv collects and stores your email (and any related
        delivery or analytics data they need to send the list) under
        <a href="https://www.beehiiv.com/privacy">Beehiiv’s privacy policy</a>. You can unsubscribe
        from the link in every email, or manage your subscription on
        <a href={SITE.beehiiv}>the Beehiiv publication</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site is a static GitHub Pages project. A Beehiiv loader script and a site-wide
        attribution script are loaded from subscribe-forms.beehiiv.com so the form can render and
        signups can be attributed. We do not run a separate analytics script at launch. Issues
        remain published on the web without a signup wall.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions and corrections</h2>
      <p>
        For a correction, takedown, or disclosure question, open an issue on the
        <a href={SITE.github}>GitHub repository</a>. Related pages:
        <a href={withBase("/about/")}>methodology</a> and the
        <a href={withBase("/issues/")}>issues archive</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
